Package: pia
Title: Pixelated Image Abstraction
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Brandon", "Monier", , "brandon.monier@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Converts high resolution images into low resolution, small palette
    outputs in the style of pixel art. Implements the method of Gerstner et al.
    (2012) "Pixelated Image Abstraction", which simultaneously solves for a
    superpixel segmentation (a modified SLIC) and a reduced color palette
    (mass-constrained deterministic annealing) in CIELAB space. The core
    optimization is implemented in Rust; results are returned as tidy tibbles
    and a 'shiny' interface is provided.
